WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.601 --> 00:00:17.751
Two weeks later, the twins were sitting in the tree house.

2
00:00:17.752 --> 00:00:22.007
"How many eyes does a bee have?" asked Katie.

3
00:00:22.008 --> 00:00:24.731
Katie was reading a book about bees.

4
00:00:24.732 --> 00:00:27.571
Joy was brushing Jellybean.

5
00:00:27.572 --> 00:00:30.605
"Two," replied Joy.

6
00:00:30.606 --> 00:00:34.088
"Five," said Katie.

7
00:00:34.089 --> 00:00:38.104
She turned the page. "Okay," she said.

8
00:00:38.105 --> 00:00:42.302
"How many times does a bee flap its wings in a minute?"

9
00:00:42.303 --> 00:00:45.597
"A thousand?" guessed Joy.

10
00:00:45.598 --> 00:00:49.851
"Twelve thousand," Katie told her.

11
00:00:49.852 --> 00:00:53.245
Katie lay down and thought about bees.

12
00:00:53.246 --> 00:00:55.719
She imagined that she was a bee.

13
00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:59.760
"I'm a sleepy bee," she thought.

14
00:00:59.761 --> 00:01:01.887
Soon she was dreaming.

15
00:01:01.888 --> 00:01:06.046
She was Katie the Bee, flapping her wings.

16
00:01:06.047 --> 00:01:10.794
Other bees flew beside her, and she could hear their wings.

17
00:01:10.795 --> 00:01:14.034
"Katie!" cried Joy.

18
00:01:14.035 --> 00:01:16.075
Katie's eyes flew open.

19
00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:19.610
The pages of her book were flapping in the wind.

20
00:01:19.611 --> 00:01:21.701
Joy stood by the window.

21
00:01:21.702 --> 00:01:24.211
Jellybean was gone.

22
00:01:24.212 --> 00:01:28.377
"The sky is turning green," Joy said.

23
00:01:28.378 --> 00:01:31.402
Dark clouds hung in the sky.

24
00:01:31.403 --> 00:01:34.046
Katie got up and looked at the wind sock.

25
00:01:34.047 --> 00:01:37.895
It was flying straight out in the wind.

26
00:01:37.896 --> 00:01:40.952
"A storm is coming," she said.

27
00:01:40.953 --> 00:01:44.952
She heard a rumble. "Thunder! Let's go."

28
00:01:44.953 --> 00:01:47.899
The girls hurried down the steps.

29
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:50.079
"Look!" shouted Joy.

30
00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:53.751
"Grandpa is trying to get the chickens in their coop."

31
00:01:53.752 --> 00:01:55.579
The girls ran to help.

32
00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:58.987
They chased the squawking birds.

33
00:01:58.988 --> 00:02:04.282
"Shoo!" they cried. Dust spun through the air.

34
00:02:04.283 --> 00:02:10.157
"Shoo!" One by one the chickens ducked through the coop door.

35
00:02:10.158 --> 00:02:13.003
"Run to the house," called Grandpa.

36
00:02:13.004 --> 00:02:15.834
"I'll be right behind you!"

37
00:02:15.835 --> 00:02:19.052
Mom was waiting on the back porch.

38
00:02:19.053 --> 00:02:23.438
"The weather service put out a tornado watch," she said.

39
00:02:23.439 --> 00:02:27.606
She held the door open and the girls rushed inside.

40
00:02:27.607 --> 00:02:31.515
The radio in the kitchen played soft music.

41
00:02:31.516 --> 00:02:34.591
"A tornado watch!" Katie cried.

42
00:02:34.592 --> 00:02:37.324
"We have to be on the lookout!"

43
00:02:37.325 --> 00:02:42.667
She grabbed her captain cap from a hook by the door and put it on.

44
00:02:42.668 --> 00:02:47.907
"This family is ready!" she declared as she went to the closet.

45
00:02:47.908 --> 00:02:52.777
She took a box from a shelf and carried it to the kitchen table.

46
00:02:52.778 --> 00:02:57.369
"Flashlight. First aid kit. Water. Snacks.

47
00:02:57.370 --> 00:03:01.123
Mom, are the pillows and blankets ready?"

48
00:03:01.124 --> 00:03:06.436
"Right here," said Mom, pointing to a basket under the table.

49
00:03:06.437 --> 00:03:10.820
"I wish Dad would come home," Joy said worriedly.

50
00:03:10.821 --> 00:03:16.481
Just as Grandpa opened the screen door, the music on the radio stopped.

51
00:03:16.482 --> 00:03:19.205
An announcer came on.

52
00:03:19.206 --> 00:03:24.256
"The National Weather Service has put out a tornado warning for Boone County.

53
00:03:24.257 --> 00:03:28.221
Current severe thunderstorms could produce a tornado.

54
00:03:28.222 --> 00:03:31.770
Towns in the warning include Willow Creek . . ."

55
00:03:31.771 --> 00:03:38.625
"A tornado warning!" shouted Katie. "That means TAKE COVER!"

56
00:03:38.626 --> 00:03:42.304
"I'll open the storm cellar," Grandpa said.

57
00:03:42.305 --> 00:03:47.231
Mom picked up her basket, and Katie picked up her box.

58
00:03:47.232 --> 00:03:50.647
"I've got the radio," said Joy.

59
00:03:50.648 --> 00:03:55.361
Outside a blast of rain and cool air hit them in the face.

60
00:03:55.362 --> 00:03:59.082
"It's so dark!" Katie said.

61
00:03:59.083 --> 00:04:04.633
"Dad!" shouted Joy as Dad's truck sped up the driveway.

62
00:04:04.634 --> 00:04:08.065
Grandpa held open the door to the storm cellar.

63
00:04:08.066 --> 00:04:10.859
"Hurry!" he called.

64
00:04:10.860 --> 00:04:14.759
"Magoo!" yelled Katie. "Come on, boy!"

65
00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:18.738
She and the dog dashed down the cellar steps.

66
00:04:18.739 --> 00:04:22.571
"Where's Jellybean?" cried Joy.

67
00:04:22.572 --> 00:04:26.270
Mom put an arm around Joy's shoulder.

68
00:04:26.271 --> 00:04:32.027
"Sorry, sweetie. There's no time to look for the cat right now," she said.

69
00:04:32.028 --> 00:04:35.420
"Oh, Jellybean . . . ," Joy whispered.

70
00:04:35.421 --> 00:04:39.524
Then she and Mom followed Katie down the steps.

71
00:04:39.525 --> 00:04:41.655
Grandpa was right behind them.

72
00:04:41.656 --> 00:04:46.707
Dad pulled the cellar door shut and fastened it tight.

73
00:04:46.708 --> 00:04:49.872
Magoo shook water from his fur.

74
00:04:49.873 --> 00:04:53.225
Mom grabbed blankets and pillows from her basket.

75
00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:56.743
"Take these," she said to the twins.

76
00:04:56.744 --> 00:05:01.015
They could hear the rain pounding on the cellar door.

77
00:05:01.016 --> 00:05:03.146
Katie hugged Magoo tight.

78
00:05:03.147 --> 00:05:06.229
Joy put a pillow over her head.

79
00:05:06.230 --> 00:05:10.859
Thunder exploded, louder and louder.

80
00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:13.777
Above them, the light bulb flashed.

81
00:05:13.778 --> 00:05:15.571
Everyone looked up.

82
00:05:15.572 --> 00:05:18.928
Then it went out.
